This thesis introduces a presentation assessment workflow for Artemis, an interactive learning platform developed at the Technical University of Munich. Since presentations are currently not directly supported in Artemis, instructors often have to rely on external tools and manual processes for organizing and grading presentations.

The goal of this work is to design and implement a flexible presentation assessment feature that supports different presentation scenarios, such as standalone presentations or presentations linked to exercises. The implementation includes configurable grading criteria, integrated assessment workflows, and integration into the existing grading system of Artemis. A particular focus is placed on usability, transparency, and a consistent user experience within the platform.